# Line endings are a CI hazard here, not a style preference.
#
# GitHub's windows-latest runners check out with core.autocrlf=true, so every
# file arrives CRLF. `cargo fmt --all --check` then compares rustfmt's LF output
# against CRLF files and fails on line endings alone — a red job that says
# nothing about the code. Shell scripts fare worse: scripts/macos-acceptance.sh
# with CRLF line endings is not runnable at all.
#
# So: normalise on commit, and check out LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary-ish things that must never be touched, in case one is ever added.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
